\tag{fdip}
\title{Finite fields and operator products}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{A field assigns a coefficient to each vertex or edge. Endpoint
pullbacks compare values on these distinct spaces, while composition
supplies an operator product on a common field module. The
[alternating four-cycle](fdip-0003) fixes coordinates and weights for
later calculations.}

\p{The coefficient ring is commutative and unital; the operator
product need not commute. Positive counting pairings and weights enter
in the [real specialization](fdip-0002). Multiplication, shifts and
discrete product rules have their own
[constructions and examples](fdip-0040).}

\transclude{fdip-0010}
